 { Find the best move for White. } 1. { -KEY- } Ne5 $1 { White needs to exchange knights, in order to avoid game-ending problems along the light squares. } ( 1. Nd2 $2 { Going after the e4 pawn would quickly lose, since after } Nxd4 2. Nxe4 $2 Nf3 3. Kh1 Qh6 $19 { Black's attack against h2 is decisive. } ) 
Nxe5 2. dxe5 Qxe5 { Black has won a pawn in the complications, but in exchange they have been left with a damaged structure and the inferior minor piece. } 3. Ne3 $11 { Black's damaged structure leaves White with compensation for the missing pawn. If Black grabs another pawn with ...Qxb2 then after Rc1 White will have excellent attacking chances on the dark squares. In this situation, the main elements were piece activity, king safety, and color complexes. } 
